{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nWhile broadening verification for runty-effectible-bluewhale on current origin/main, `tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_preview_under_sync_contention_heldout.py::test_preview_is_complete_while_sync_locks_are_held` failed deterministically, both in the 443-test store suite and alone. `_advisory_lock._lock_remote` imports `from rebar_reconciler import git_adapter`, but that top-level package is intentionally unavailable in the normal installed in-process environment, raising `ModuleNotFoundError` before the lock behavior executes. This is unrelated to attach-commits code-root changes.\n\n## Confirmed Root Cause\nCommit `d9e0f0e733` introduced unconditional top-level `git_adapter` imports at `_advisory_lock.py:83` and `_ref_lock.py:194`, breaking the explicit standalone by-path loading contract in `_advisory_lock.py` and `_loader.py`. Runtime experiments confirmed both failure sites; the pre-refactor parent succeeds with the same absent top-level package; supported package-seeded paths remain green. The full proof is recorded in the Phase 1 RCA comment.\n\n## Repair Plan\n- Route `git_adapter` loading at both confirmed seams through the existing standalone-safe `lazy_load` sibling loader, preserving the canonical cache-key contract.\n- Preserve package-loaded behavior, adapter API identity, lock semantics, and intentional wheel packaging.\n- Do not change the interface oracle or add test-only `sys.path`/package seeding.\n\n## Testing\n- Use the existing failing held-out interface test as the RED oracle because it crosses both real standalone load seams and exercises a real ref-lock acquire/check/release around bridge preview.\n- Hold the oracle out from the fixer, then require GREEN; mutate each repaired seam back to the exact absolute import and require RED; restore and require GREEN.\n- Run the exact original reproduction, advisory/ref-lock tests, the broader store interface suite, and project lint/typecheck gates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The exact held-out contention test passes in isolation without test-only path pollution.\n- [ ] Both standalone git-adapter seams use the supported sibling-loader contract while package-loaded execution remains valid.\n- [ ] Defect-seeded mutation of either seam returns the held-out oracle to RED.\n- [ ] The broader store suite passes.\n- [ ] Lint and typecheck pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787046269320020001,"uuid":"c98c4083-59c6-46ec-a15f-a547f1fb63f5"}